<.layout_page_centered>
  <!-- Project header -->
  <.container_page_heading
    title="FONTDUE.COM"
    description="Reporting, preview and invoicing engines for 100+ independent type foundries"
  />
  <!-- Brand hero image -->
  <.container_hero_image image="/images/cases/fontdue_about.png" />
  <!-- About company -->
  <.container_page_text title="The Company">
    <.container_page_paragraph>
      <.link_styled href="https://www.fontdue.com">Fontdue</.link_styled>
      is an ecommerce platform built exclusively for independent type foundries. Since 2018 it has powered 100+ foundries worldwide — including ArrowType, Fort Foundry and Letterror — handling catalog management, font licensing, <.link_styled href="https://stripe.com/">Stripe</.link_styled> payments, webfont generation, and a JavaScript component library (Fontdue.js) for type testers, cart and checkout.
    </.container_page_paragraph>
    <.container_page_paragraph>
      Fontdue is white-label by design — the foundry's brand stays front and centre. It is purpose-built where generic platforms like <.link_styled href="https://www.shopify.com/">Shopify</.link_styled> fall short: variable fonts, OpenType features, multi-variable licensing and trial fonts are all first-class concepts.
    </.container_page_paragraph>
  </.container_page_text>

<!-- About project -->
  <.container_page_text title="The project">
    <.container_page_paragraph>
      Fontdue is a mature platform with a global foundry customer base. Our engagement focused on <b>quality-of-life improvements</b> — features that move shop owners from "can I make this work?" to "this is exactly the data and tooling I need."
    </.container_page_paragraph>
    <.container_page_paragraph>
      We delivered three workstreams with Fontdue's core team:
      <ul>
        <.container_page_paragraph_item icon="hero-check">
          a <b>reporting & analytics system</b>
          for shop income, sales velocity, top-performing fonts and license mix
        </.container_page_paragraph_item>
        <.container_page_paragraph_item icon="hero-check">
          a <b>font preview mechanism</b>
          for verifying how fonts and families present to customers before publishing
        </.container_page_paragraph_item>
        <.container_page_paragraph_item icon="hero-check">
          <b>invoice generation improvements and data export</b>
          for accounting, tax filing and customer support
        </.container_page_paragraph_item>
      </ul>
    </.container_page_paragraph>
    <.container_page_paragraph>
      Each improvement slots into Fontdue's existing admin with no breaking changes and no disruption to foundries already on the platform.
    </.container_page_paragraph>
  </.container_page_text>
  <!--Quote -->
  <.container_page_card
    description="Remote Reason's work has provided quality-of-life improvements and unlocked new sales potential for the client's end customers. The team has delivered on time, onboarded quickly, and communicated through texts and video calls.
    Their autonomy and problem-solving skills have impressed the client."
    image={LinkHelper.image_path("/cases/tom.jpeg")}
    name="Tom Conroy"
    position="CEO & Founder, Fontdue"
    clutch="https://clutch.co/profile/remote-reason#review-381654?utm_campaign=widget&utm_content=testimonial&utm_medium=8&utm_source=widget&utm_term=localhost"
  />
  <!--Showcase -->
  <div class="container px-6 lg:px-12">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold leading-normal text-left md:text-4xl">
      What we delivered
    </h1>
  </div>
  <!-- Reporting -->
  <.container_box_large
    alignment="left"
    image="/images/cases/fontdue_graph.png"
    title="Reporting system with Apache ECharts"
  >
    Foundries could see individual orders but had no way to ask higher-level questions about their business. We built a reporting module powered by <.link_styled href="https://echarts.apache.org/">Apache ECharts</.link_styled>.
    <ul>
      <.container_page_paragraph_item title="Revenue dashboards">
        Gross revenue, net of fees, by day, week, month or custom range with period comparisons.
      </.container_page_paragraph_item>
      <.container_page_paragraph_item title="Sales volume & velocity">
        Orders per day, units sold per font, conversion across the catalog.
      </.container_page_paragraph_item>
      <.container_page_paragraph_item title="Top-performing fonts & families">
        Ranked tables and charts of top collections, families and styles by revenue.
      </.container_page_paragraph_item>
      <.container_page_paragraph_item title="License mix analytics">
        Distribution of license types, variable selections and average order value per tier.
      </.container_page_paragraph_item>
      <.container_page_paragraph_item title="Geographic & currency breakdown">
        Sales by country and currency, including Purchasing Power Parity pricing.
      </.container_page_paragraph_item>
      <.container_page_paragraph_item title="Interactive filtering">
        Filter by date, collection, license and currency, with CSV export.
      </.container_page_paragraph_item>
    </ul>
  </.container_box_large>
  <.lets_talk_cta />
  <!-- Font preview -->
  <.container_box_large
    alignment="right"
    image="/images/cases/fontdue_font.png"
    title="Font preview mechanism for shop owners"
  >
    Foundries upload fonts continuously and need to confirm what the customer will see before hitting publish. We built an internal preview tool that renders the live catalog with full QA controls.
    <ul>
      <.container_page_paragraph_item title="Family- and collection-level previews">
        Every style in a family side-by-side, with waterfall and per-style toggles.
      </.container_page_paragraph_item>
      <.container_page_paragraph_item title="Variable font axis controls">
        Interactive sliders for every registered axis (weight, width, optical size, custom).
      </.container_page_paragraph_item>
      <.container_page_paragraph_item title="OpenType feature inspection">
        Toggle stylistic sets, alternates, ligatures and numerals before publishing.
      </.container_page_paragraph_item>
      <.container_page_paragraph_item title="Glyph & character coverage view">
        Visual confirmation of glyphs and Unicode ranges per file.
      </.container_page_paragraph_item>
      <.container_page_paragraph_item title="Side-by-side version comparison">
        Preview updated files against the current published version to catch regressions.
      </.container_page_paragraph_item>
      <.container_page_paragraph_item title="Trial vs. retail comparison">
        See how the trial font differs from the retail file customers receive.
      </.container_page_paragraph_item>
    </ul>
  </.container_box_large>
  <!-- Invoices -->
  <.container_box_large
    alignment="left"
    image="/images/cases/fontdue_doc.png"
    title="Invoice generation & data export"
  >
    Invoices connect Fontdue to a foundry's accounting and tax workflows. We rebuilt the invoice pipeline and added bulk export to remove monthly copy-paste work.
    <ul>
      <.container_page_paragraph_item title="Redesigned PDF invoices">
        Brand-consistent layout with foundry and customer details, license breakdown, currency, tax and <.link_styled href="https://stripe.com/">Stripe</.link_styled>
        reference.
      </.container_page_paragraph_item>
      <.container_page_paragraph_item title="Multi-currency & tax-compliant">
        VAT/sales tax line items via <.link_styled href="https://stripe.com/tax">Stripe Tax</.link_styled>, with country-specific formatting for EU e-invoicing.
      </.container_page_paragraph_item>
      <.container_page_paragraph_item title="License-aware line items">
        Each license appears with its variable selections (e.g. <em>Desktop, 11–50 employees, example.com</em>).
      </.container_page_paragraph_item>
      <.container_page_paragraph_item title="Bulk regeneration">
        Reissue invoices in batch when foundry details change, without touching individual orders.
      </.container_page_paragraph_item>
      <.container_page_paragraph_item title="Data export for accounting">
        One-click CSV/Excel export of orders, customers and revenue, ready for Xero / QuickBooks / accountants.
      </.container_page_paragraph_item>
      <.container_page_paragraph_item title="Customer-facing invoice retrieval">
        Buyers can re-download invoices from the login form, eliminating inbound tickets.
      </.container_page_paragraph_item>
    </ul>
  </.container_box_large>
  <!-- Project Highlights  -->
  <.container_page_text title="Highlights" />
  <.container_page_box>
    <.page_box_items title="Project">
      <p class="font-semibold">
        Sector: <span class="font-normal">E-commerce / SaaS for type foundries </span>
      </p>
      <p class="font-semibold">
        Work: <span class="font-normal">Backend, Frontend, Data visualisation </span>
      </p>
      <p class="font-semibold">
        Size: <span class="font-normal"> > 300h </span>
      </p>
    </.page_box_items>
    <.page_box_items title="Verticals">
      <p>- E-commerce</p>
      <p>- Type design & font distribution</p>
      <p>- Reporting & analytics</p>
      <p>- Invoicing & financial operations</p>
    </.page_box_items>
    <.page_box_items title="Technologies">
      <p>- <.tech_icon name="js" /> JavaScript / <.tech_icon name="react" /> React</p>
      <p>- <.tech_icon name="echarts" /> Apache ECharts</p>
      <p>- <.tech_icon name="graphql" /> GraphQL</p>
      <p>- <.tech_icon name="stripe" /> Stripe</p>
      <p>- <.tech_icon name="pdf" /> PDF</p>
      <p>- <.tech_icon name="csv" /> CSV / Excel</p>
    </.page_box_items>
  </.container_page_box>
</.layout_page_centered>
